course: dictionary
lesson: 13370
title: Hasten: a formal word for hurry
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hasten is a formal word. It means to hurry, or to make something happen sooner. Writers use it in stories and serious writing where hurry might sound too everyday. «She hastened home before the rain started.» She went home quickly, so hastened means hurried.
explain: Hasten can also mean making something happen sooner. «Rain hastened the end of the game.» The rain did not stop the game slowly. It made the game finish earlier than it would have. Ask yourself: did something happen faster, or did someone move faster? Either way, hasten means sooner or quicker.
explain: Watch for the phrase «hasten to add». «I hasten to add that the cake was only a little burnt.» Here it means you quickly say something so people do not get the wrong idea. You will meet this phrase in grown-up writing and speeches.
fact: Hasten means to hurry, or to make something happen sooner.
fact: «Hasten» is a formal word, so you will see it more in stories and serious writing than in everyday talk.
fact: Hasten is a verb. Its other forms are hastens, hastened and hastening.
fact: «Hasten to add» or «hasten to say» means you quickly say something to stop a wrong idea.
fact: For the meanings hurry and sooner, you can test your idea by putting hurry or sooner into the sentence and checking that it still makes sense.
exercise: «The nurse hastened to the room when the bell rang.» What does hastened mean here? | Walked very slowly | Sang loudly | *Hurried | Forgot the way
exercise: «Rain hastened the end of the game.» Find and copy the word that means made something happen sooner. | *hastened | end | game | rain
exercise: «I hasten to add that the cake was only a little burnt.» What does hasten to add mean? | You run to the kitchen | You add sugar to the cake very fast | *You quickly say something so people do not get the wrong idea | You hurry to finish the cake
test: «The bus was late, so we hastened to the stop.» What does hastened mean? | *Hurried | Fell asleep | Ate lunch | Stayed still
test: «Warm weather will hasten the melting of the snow.» What does hasten mean here? | *Made it happen sooner | Covered up | Slowed down | Stopped completely
exam: Ava says hasten means to slow down. What does hasten really mean? | To be quiet and still | To look up at the sky | *To hurry, or to make something happen sooner | To stop for a rest
